    "senderName": "NWS Great Falls MT",
    "headline": "High Wind Warning issued October 16 at 6:06PM MDT until October 18 at 12:00AM MDT by NWS Great Falls MT",
    "description": "* WHAT...Westerly winds 30 to 50 mph with gusts up to 85 mph\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...East Glacier Park Region Zone, and Eastern Glacier, Western\nToole, and Central Pondera, Northern High Plains, Southern High\nPlains, and Southern Rocky Mountain Front.\n\n* WHEN...From 9 AM Saturday to midnight MDT Saturday Night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel will be difficult, especially for high profile\nvehicles. Isolated instances of tree damage and or power outages\nare possible.\n\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The strong winds will also bring difficult\nconditions for outdoor recreation in portions of Glacier National\nPark, particularly over and near higher terrain on the eastern side\nof the Park.",
    "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind.",
    "response": "Prepare",
